      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "The hypothesis is empty, but the target chain indicates a research objective to validate \"rigid probe feasibility in solution space\" via theoretical proof, numerical simulation, and comparison with flexible probes. This is an open-ended exploration of parameter space (probe geometry, solution space constraints, noise levels) to identify optimal configurations and performance boundaries. I will use the explore mode to generate multiple hypotheses on probe design, run asynchronous simulations (e.g., via symbolic_math_tool for theoretical bounds and numerical_tool for coverage efficiency), apply Pareto pruning, and report the Pareto front with reasons for pruning/retention. This aligns with the \"Exploration Mode\" directive for open-ended queries and ensures methodological rigor by cross-validating against domain knowledge (e.g., convergence, physical reasonableness)."
    },
