      "value": "Pareto front of probe designs showing trade-offs between coverage efficiency (e.g., % of solution space covered) and robustness (e.g., success rate under noise). Expected outcome: rigid probes may show higher coverage in low-noise, convex solution spaces but degrade sharply in high-noise or non-convex regions; flexible probes may offer better robustness at lower coverage. Specific metrics: coverage efficiency ~0.6-0.9 for rigid probes in ideal conditions, robustness drop >50% when noise amplitude >0.1 units."
